# Dependency binary source policy.
#
# npm packages: resolved sources in package-lock.json MUST come from the
# official registry (https://registry.npmjs.org) — enforced in CI by
# scripts/check-lockfile-registry.mjs. Do not commit lockfiles recorded against
# other registries.
#
# Electron / electron-builder binaries: production artifacts are built from
# official sources (Electron releases on github.com, electron-builder binaries
# from their upstream). Restricted networks that need a mirror MUST inject it
# per-environment via environment variables (ELECTRON_MIRROR and
# ELECTRON_BUILDER_BINARIES_MIRROR) — never through committed config, so a
# committed checkout always resolves to official sources. The previous
# electron_mirror / electron_builder_binaries_mirror keys were removed: npm
# warns they are unknown project config and they pinned builds to an
# unapproved mirror.
